<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  Universal Converter converts files on the phone and sends no file anywhere (PRIVACY.md). Files
  are read in the app, the results are saved through the share sheet
  (@unisim/media/save: @capacitor/filesystem writes to the app's cache, then
  @capacitor/share), and they are gone when the app closes.

  Updated 2026-11-21: the phone app recognises a suite sign-in. It was
  "Data Not Collected" from 2026-10-12 (privacy audit). What it collects now, and only when the
  phone already holds a UNI·SIM session that ANOTHER suite app made (the
  shared Keychain group co.uk.unisim.suite on iOS, the suite's shared sign-in
  on Android):

  - No sign-in of its own. The phone build sets @unisim/sdk's `noAccounts`
    and `signInInTune: false` (src/main.tsx): no Sign in, no account screens,
    no name or email on screen, no "the app was opened" event (there is no
    <UsageTracker />). It reads the session the device holds and follows it.
  - User ID, linked, App Functionality: the account id the session carries,
    which keys the reads and writes below.
  - Other Data Types, linked, App Functionality: Tune this app's choices are
    kept with the account and read back on its other devices, in
    `user_app_prefs`: this app's own colour scheme and language,
    and the tab it opens on,
    in the `tune:converter` row (the SDK's TuneSync), the suite-wide colour scheme
    and language in the `suite` row (with the list of suite apps the account
    has used). The phone's tab order goes the same way, in its own
    `tune-app:converter` row (src/native/tabOrder.ts, the SDK's
    createSyncedSettings).

  - Name, linked, App Functionality: the name the person goes by in the
    suite ("Call me", Global Tuning) follows the account in its own
    `suite-call-me` row. The phone app never shows it, but when the account
    has none and the phone's shared suite settings hold one, the SDK saves it
    to the account, so it is declared.

  Email Address is not declared: the phone app neither shows nor sends it
  (its bar has no personal title).

  Nothing else changes: no file leaves the phone, and no usage count (the
  suite user count, an install id every 45 s, was retired in @unisim/sdk
  0.187.0, and its replacement, the anonymous daily open count, is off under
  `noAccounts` and, in the iOS/Android shell, also under src/main.tsx
  `openCount: !Capacitor.isNativePlatform()`, because the App Store and Play
  figures already count installs). Nothing is used for tracking. Signed out,
  the only network requests are the changelog (changelog.unisim.co.uk) and
  the app's own update check, neither of which carries anything about the
  user.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem's native code reads file
  creation and modification dates (its `stat`), only for files in the app's
  own container, and the plugin ships no manifest of its own, so C617.1 is
  declared here. Capacitor's core frameworks carry their own manifests.

  Keep this in step with store-assets/data-safety.json, the App Store
  Connect privacy answers (Name, User ID and Other Data Types: linked, not tracking,
  App Functionality; see Docs_UNI_SIM/store-listings/universal-converter.md) and PRIVACY.md.
  Written 2026-10-12 (privacy audit), updated 2026-11-21.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- "Call me": the SDK may save the phone's one to the account. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- The account id a suite session on the phone carries. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Tune this app settings kept with the account. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
